.TH SHOT 1 "2026-11-08" "holyc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shot \- screenshot, screen recording and area selection for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shot
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMODE\fR]
.br
.B shot rec
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIMODE\fR]
.br
.B shot sel
.br
.B shot \-l
.SH DESCRIPTION
Takes a screenshot (default), starts or stops a screen recording, or lets you drag an area and prints it as
.IR "X,Y WxH" .
Running
.B shot rec
a second time stops the recording, so it can be bound to one key.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B full
every screen together (default)
.TP
.B output
one screen: \fB\-o\fR NAME, or the selected screen under dwl
.TP
.B area
drag a rectangle
.TP
.B window
the focused window (dwl, from its control socket)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-o \fINAME\fR
which screen (implies output)
.TP
.B \-f \fIFILE\fR
write to FILE instead of ~/Pictures/shot-DATE.png
.TP
.B \-d \fISEC\fR
wait before capturing
.TP
.B \-c
clipboard only, no file
.TP
.B \-n
no clipboard copy and no notification
.TP
.B \-a
(rec) record audio too
.TP
.B \-l
list the screens
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/shot.rec
pid and file of the running recorder.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dwl.sock
dwl control socket, used to find screens and the focused window.
.SH REQUIRES
grim, slurp, wf-recorder, wl-copy, and optionally notify-send.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notts (1),
.BR scenario (1)
